# Iconography

## Size tokens (required)

Canonical Foundation tokens live in `packages/ui/src/foundations/iconography.css`. Components **must** size icons with these — never hardcoded px, `size-4` / `size-6`, or ad-hoc values.

| Token | px |
|---|---|
| `--icon-2xs` | 8 |
| `--icon-xs` | 12 |
| `--icon-sm` | 16 |
| `--icon-md` | 20 |
| `--icon-lg` | 24 |
| `--icon-xl` | 32 |
| `--icon-2xl` | 40 |
| `--icon-3xl` | 48 |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — Tailwind defaults / literals
<Icon className="size-4" />
<svg width={16} height={16} />

// ✅ GOOD — Foundation icon size tokens
<Icon className="size-[length:var(--icon-sm)]" />
<Icon style={{ width: 'var(--icon-sm)', height: 'var(--icon-sm)' }} />
// Solar: pass resolved px to `size` if CSS vars are not accepted
```

Typical mapping when adapting shadcn: `size-3`/`size-4` → `--icon-sm` (or `--icon-xs` for dense badges), `size-5` → `--icon-md`, `size-6` → `--icon-lg`.

## Icon sets (not CSS tokens)

Individual glyphs are **library components**, not CSS design tokens:

- **Lucide** (`lucide-react`) — primary system UI (buttons, inputs, nav, alerts, badges)
- **Solar Bold Duotone** (`@solar-icons/react`, `weight="BoldDuotone"`) — illustrations / empty states / Lucide gaps only

Solar secondary (lighter) duotone layers use `--icon-solar-secondary-opacity`
(**0.2** / 20%). Full-opacity paths stay 100%. Wrap the tree in `FabelySolarProvider`
(`packages/ui/src/foundations/solar-provider.tsx`) so SVGs get
`data-fabely-solar` — Storybook preview already does.

Catalog: Storybook → Foundations → Iconography → Icon Library → Lucide | Solar | Fabely Icons.

Do not mix Lucide and Solar in the same interface. Prefer `currentColor` so icons inherit text / disabled styles.

## shadcn / vendor components

When adding or wrapping shadcn under `packages/ui`:

1. Replace hardcoded icon sizes with `--icon-*` tokens immediately.
2. Keep Lucide as the icon library (`components.json` → `iconLibrary: "lucide"`).
3. Public Fabely atoms wrap vendor primitives and own the tokenized icon sizing — do not leave `size-4` in Fabely-facing APIs.
